Based on the technical whitepaper and foundry brief for the Telemetry Photonic Integrated Circuit (TPIC) (DWG TPIC-ARCH-CMB-001 Rev 4.2), here is a structured summary of the architecture specifications, generated parameters, real-data potentials, detection results, and boundary statuses:
1. Device Summary & Architecture
 * Circuit Type: Five-layer silicon-on-insulator (SOI) photonic integrated circuit.
 * Data Bus Applications: Astrophysics observational telemetry, including spectral flux density arrays, pulsar timing telemetry, and gravitational-wave interferometer inputs.
 * Layer Architecture:
   * Layer 1 (Photonic): SOI waveguides, Mach-Zehnder modulator array, and tunable ring resonators.
   * Layer 2 (Quantum Module): Quantum Key Distribution (QKD) photon encryption module and tunable rings.
   * Layer 3 (Control & Logic): Resonator filter bank.
   * Layer 4 (Interconnect & Routing): Photodetector arrays and grating couplers.
   * Layer 5: Substrate / CMOS.
 * Additional Integrated Features: Entangled-pair source with a QKD logic core, data encryption & routing, thermal phase shifters, a Through-Silicon Via (TSV) array, laser-diode coupling (external laser input, fiber V-groove), and a 169-ball grid array pinout.
 * Material Legend: Si, \text{SiO}_2, Metal, Quantum Substrate. (Note: TPIC stands alone and is distinct from TC-001 [EQS-580], PTCE-001, and the Blackwell Light Chip [EQS-1046]).
